.TH VRGB 1 "September 2026" "vivobook-rgb" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vrgb \- control the RGB keyboard of ASUS Vivobook laptops via HID LampArray
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrgb
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vrgb
controls the RGB lighting of ASUS Vivobook keyboards that use the ITE5570
HID LampArray controller (e.g. M5606KA, S5406SA) by talking to the
controller directly through the Linux hidraw subsystem \[em] no WMI, no
kernel modules.
.PP
The ITE5570 exposes the keyboard as a single lamp (one zone), so the whole
keyboard shares one color. Per-key control is not possible on this hardware.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B info
Show lamp array information (lamp count, kind, minimum update interval).
.TP
.B color \fICOLOR\fR [\fIBRIGHTNESS\fR]
Set a solid color for the whole keyboard.
\fICOLOR\fR is 6 hex digits (RRGGBB) or a name (see COLORS below).
\fIBRIGHTNESS\fR is 0-255, default 255.
.TP
.B off
Turn the LEDs off.
.TP
.B auto
Re-enable the firmware autonomous (rainbow) mode.
.TP
.B effect breathe \fICOLOR\fR [\fIPERIOD\fR]
Pulse \fICOLOR\fR breathing in and out. \fIPERIOD\fR is seconds per cycle,
default 4.
.TP
.B effect cycle [\fIPERIOD\fR]
Continuously cycle through the HSV color wheel in software. \fIPERIOD\fR
is seconds per full wheel, default 8.
.TP
.B effect fade \fICOLOR\fR [\fIDURATION\fR]
Fade from the current color to \fICOLOR\fR. \fIDURATION\fR is seconds,
default 1.
.TP
.B daemon
Run in the foreground watching the state file
.IR ~/.cache/vrgb/state.json .
Whenever the file changes, the new state is applied \[em] including live
effect switching. Stop with Ctrl+C.
.TP
.B set \fIMODE\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
Write the state file consumed by
.BR "vrgb daemon" .
Modes: \fBcolor \fICOLOR\fR [\fIBRIGHTNESS\fR]\fR, \fBoff\fR, \fBauto\fR,
\fBbreathe \fICOLOR\fR [\fIPERIOD\fR]\fR, \fBcycle\fR [\fIPERIOD\fR]\fR,
\fBfade \fICOLOR\fR [\fIDURATION\fR]\fR.
.SH COLORS
Wherever a color is expected, either 6 hex digits (RRGGBB, with optional
leading \fB#\fR) or one of these names is accepted:
.BR red ", " green ", " blue ", " yellow ", " cyan ", " magenta ", "
.BR orange ", " purple ", " pink ", " white ", " warmwhite ", " black "."
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/vrgb/state.json
State file consumed by
.BR daemon .
.TP
.I /etc/vrgb.conf
Default color/brightness applied by vrgb-default.service on boot and
after resume.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero on error (device not found, permission denied,
invalid arguments).
